{"document_id": "917e50b0-bc3f-4b96-9c9c-8d0593cd110c", "crop": "mango", "organization": "TNAU", "source": "TNAU", "source_url": "https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/crop_prot_postharvest_mango_3.html", "title": "TNAU Agritech Portal :: Crop Protection", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-06T23:40:56.413268", "content": "| ![TNAU Agritech Portal](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/index/cp_index.jpg)  |  \n| --- |  \n|  [Home](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/index.html \"Home\") | [About Us](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/about_us/abt_us.html \"About Us\") | [Success Stories](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/success_stories/success_index.html \"Success Stories\") | [Farmers Association](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_association/farm_assoct.html \"Farmer's Association\") | [Farmers' Innovation](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/farm_innovations/farm_innovations.html) | [Publications](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/tnau_publish.html \"TNAU Publications\") | [Contact](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/contact.html \"Contact Us\")  |   |  \n|  Post Harvest Diseases :: Fruits :: Mango  \n |  **_Diplodia_ stem end rot:  _Diplodia natalensis_** **Symptoms:**\n  * Epicarp darkens around the base - pedicel.\n  * Circular, black patch which under humid atmosphere.\n  * Soft rot –aid of pectinolytic & cellulolytic enzymes.\n  * More portions of fruit turns black and soften.\n  * Lose ascorbic acid & non- reducing sugars rapidly\n\n**Mode of spread and survival:**\n  * The fungus persists in infected plant parts which serve as source of inoculum\n\n**Epidemiology:**\n  * RH – 80%, max.& min.temp. of 31.5 and 25.90C.\n\n |   \n | ![](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/crop_protection/images/posthar_mango/diplodiastem_end_rot_1.jpg)  |  \n| --- |  \n| **_Diplodia_ stem end rot**  |  \n |  \n |  \n| \n* * *\n[Home](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/index.html \"Home\") | [About Us](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/about_us/abt_us.html \"About Us\") | [Success Stories](https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/success_stor